    "result_text": "The full suite passes (14 tests, 0 failures), including the new `Cp07Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the registration-date default for `POST /api/owners` end-to-end:\n\n1. **OpenAPI schema** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since `Owner` includes `OwnerFields` via `allOf`, this makes the field bindable on the request DTO and returned on the response DTO, and the OpenAPI generator produces it as a `LocalDate` \u2014 which Jackson serializes in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` form. MapStruct maps it by name automatically in both directions.\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added a `registrationDate` `LocalDate` field mapped to a `registration_date DATE` column, with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`BuildOwner` function** \u2014 after mapping the request to the entity, it defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when the request supplied none, preserving any supplied value. This keeps the default a server-side concern in the pipeline's build step.\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table in all four schemas (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres); hsqldb is the one the test suite uses (`ddl-auto=none`, schema driven by `schema.sql`).\n\nBoth new tests pass: `coreDefaultsToToday` (defaults to server's current date) and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` (an explicit `2020-06-15` round-trips unchanged), and no existing tests regressed.",
